# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows workstations, and git decides text vs
# binary by looking for a NUL byte in the first 8 KB. That guess is per file:
# a baked .hdr or .bin whose header happens to be plain ASCII can be judged
# "text", and git then rewrites every LF to CRLF and silently corrupts it.
#
# The renderer would not error on a corrupted pack, it would just draw wrong.
# So the pipeline's output formats are pinned rather than guessed.
*.glb   binary
*.bin   binary
*.webp  binary
*.hdr   binary
*.ktx2  binary
*.vtex  binary
*.vpk   binary
*.dem   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
